  "Scenes.Alicescene.AliceEncounterBossy.LeapingOutPointingFace": "[pg]Leaping out and pointing toward your [face], the apparent child that was hiding sternly questions you. [say: What are you doing out [if (!isday) {this late|here}]!? It's dangerous to be wandering the wilderness!] Her human looks and [aliceskin] skin are as disarming as her youthful and small frame--no taller than [if (height>52 || height<47) {a child back home|you}], [if (height<47) {though still noticeably taller than you|give or take}]. [say: Are you lost?] the young girl asks. You read mild annoyance in her expression, but it occurs to you that, really, you should be the one asking that. [say: [if (height<51 || isChild) {Am I to ignore some kid aimlessly walking the [areaname]? I'm the older one here!|You don't have a clue where you're going! You're a mess of a person that's going to die of starvation under a rock somewhere.}]] Having clearly no patience for a response, the girl grabs you by the hand and starts pulling you alongside her. Immediate warmth spreads through you at the point of contact, "
  "Scenes.Alicescene.AliceEncounterBossy.MindClicksSensesAlice": "and at once your mind clicks to its senses to see the Alice for what she is."
